{0 IMAP for OCaml and Eio}

{!modules: Imap Imap_eio Imap_store Imap_sync}

The [imap] package is an IMAP4rev1 and IMAP4rev2 client with a durable
IMAP to Maildir synchronizer and the [imap-sync] command.

{1 Libraries}

[imap], whose module is {!Imap}, holds the protocol values, response
framing and parsing, command encoders, the extension vocabularies, and
the scan and reconciliation planners. It performs no I/O.

[imap.eio], whose module is {!Imap_eio}, runs the protocol over Eio.
{!Imap_eio.Auth} and {!Imap_eio.Transport} describe a login and an
endpoint, {!Imap_eio.Client} is one authenticated connection,
{!Imap_eio.Selected} is a mailbox selection lease, and {!Imap_eio.Pool}
bounds a set of connections.

[imap.store], whose module is {!Imap_store}, keeps SQLite cursors and
UID snapshots, the pair and operation journal, and a content-addressed
archive of message bodies.

[maildir], a separate package whose module is {!Maildir}, stores
messages in the Dovecot Maildir layout. It depends on no IMAP library.

[imap.sync], whose modules are under [Imap_sync], synchronizes one
mailbox with one Maildir. {!Imap_sync.Ctx} binds a connection, a store
and a mailbox. {!Imap_sync.Engine} scans, archives and appends,
{!Imap_sync.Bridge} runs a cycle in both directions,
{!Imap_sync.Flags} and {!Imap_sync.Deletion} reconcile one pair,
{!Imap_sync.Plan} previews a cycle offline, {!Imap_sync.Repair} holds the
operator repairs, and {!Imap_sync.Watch} reacts to IDLE. Every call
reports one {!Imap_sync.Error.t}.

{1 Layering}

[imap] depends only on [mail-flag]. [imap.eio] and [imap.store] each
depend on [imap] and not on each other. [maildir] stands alone.
[imap.sync] depends on all four and is the only library that performs
both network and local storage I/O. A program that speaks IMAP without
synchronizing links [imap.eio] alone.

{1 Extensions}

{!Imap.Capability.t} types each capability token, and
{!Imap_eio.Client.capabilities} and {!Imap_eio.Client.enabled} are the
sets the server advertised and ENABLE confirmed. An operation that exists
only because of an extension lives in a submodule named for it, such as
{!Imap_eio.Selected.Move} on a lease or {!Imap_eio.Client.Quota} on a
connection. The submodule's [require] checks the capability once and
returns a witness that its operations take in place of the lease or
client. A missing extension [c] is [Error (Unsupported c)] and a mode
that ENABLE has not confirmed is [Error (Not_enabled c)], both
constructors of {!Imap_eio.Error.t}. Neither sends anything, so a
fallback is one match arm. [require] succeeds where effective IMAP4rev2
folds the extension in, and a lease witness expires with its lease.

{1 Guides}

{!page-client} connects, searches, fetches and moves messages with a
fallback for servers without MOVE. {!page-sync} runs one durable sync
cycle and reads its receipt. Their programs live under
[test/examples/], which the build compiles and never runs.
